{:edb/db-before-t 1499 :edb/db-after-t 1500 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534812 50 #inst "2026-10-08T07:50:01.113Z" 13194139534812 true] [17592186198057 1100 "Given that $P(A)=\\dfrac12$, $P(A \\cap B)=\\dfrac16$, and $P(A \\cup B)=\\dfrac23$, find $P(A'\\cup B')$." 13194139534812 false] [17592186198057 1100 "Given that $P(A)=\\dfrac12,$ $P(A \\cap B)=\\dfrac16,$ and $P(A \\cup B)=\\dfrac23,$ find $P(A'\\cup B').$" 13194139534812 true] [17592186198057 1145 "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(A∪B) &= P(A) + P(B) - P(A∩B) \\\\\n\\frac{2}{3} &= \\frac{1}{2} + P(B) - \\frac{1}{6} \\\\\nP(B) &= \\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{1}{6} - \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\nP(B) &= \\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A'\\cup B'$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4315/Source/Images/dfa6d853388443970cef0fa6c14c69db.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A'\\cup B') = \\dfrac1{3} + \\dfrac{1}{6} + \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac56\n$$" 13194139534812 false] [17592186198057 1145 "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}+P(B)-\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(B) & =\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ P(B) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A'\\cup B'.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/9856c9b0fdf3bf4b8f84417f6e625d823590f57dac4dcc8185994aef3f8c5e50.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A'\\cup B') = \\dfrac1{3} + \\dfrac{1}{6} + \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac56.\n$$" 13194139534812 true] [17592186198067 1100 "Given $P(A)=0.3$, $P(B)=0.5$, and $P(A\\cup B)=0.7$, find $P(A'\\cap B)$." 13194139534812 false] [17592186198067 1100 "Given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/ca3ae8f8df5bb20c40261cb25dbfdcf31a71717c01b6ef820c5c5ded2aedbbfc.png), ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/6071a2687c038fe8b7e95abe89c07b93aebe21424fadde72eb5ac52e64771895.png), ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/6a2c9b8bfdd3b9c0f642c1a96f8914926a2ef7c2f0aacdc536cee42760a63448.png), find ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/7ca88e3705a778b7a8329a2a7ae3248a377a79aa2a88bee51e7360dd36536e82.png)" 13194139534812 true] [17592186198067 1145 "First, we calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/9b7b7cbb7f22bed24e5dafdfdbb4e29cc434eaeeb361ac601673654299dfedd0.png) using the addition law\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/8ac1b158770eacf57e651320b9aff02492fa6693383cd5c07c43fbcf439a3141.png)\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/8951b2f0456d6317f684dba75a4eb098bfeeb6fa77ec83947d4e2f09baadaece.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/bac5655a5b79a32e8155e26be50275409a6bbf41b939cfb823e5e53fccef6663.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/dc3c94937b19dc1efda8aa5356c0985fc6833d85cdfa1437a5fc60c88e018de9.png)" 13194139534812 true] [17592186198067 1145 "First, we calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(A∪B) &= P(A) + P(B) - P(A∩B) \\\\\n0.7 &= 0.3 + 0.5 - P(A∩B) \\\\\nP(A∩B) &= 0.3 + 0.5 - 0.7 \\\\\nP(A∩B) &= 0.1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A'\\cap B$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4315/Source/Images/cb945eebe175b9cf96e1be4d308d32d0.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A'\\cap B) = 0.4\n$$" 13194139534812 false] [17592186198068 1100 "Given that $P(B)=0.6$, $P(A\\cap B)=0.4$, and $P(A\\cup B)=0.9$, find $P(A')$." 13194139534812 false] [17592186198068 1100 "Given that $P(B)=0.6,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.4,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.9,$ find $P(A').$" 13194139534812 true] [17592186198068 1145 "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(A∪B) &= P(A) + P(B) - P(A∩B) \\\\\n0.9 &= P(A) + 0.6 - 0.4 \\\\\nP(A) &= 0.9 + 0.4 - 0.6 \\\\\nP(A) &= 0.7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(A^{′}) &= 1 - P(A) \\\\\n&= 1 - 0.7 \\\\\n&= 0.3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534812 false] [17592186198068 1145 "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.9 & =P(A)+0.6-0.4 \\\\ P(A) & =0.9+0.4-0.6 \\\\ P(A) & =0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}) & =1-P(A) \\\\  & =1-0.7 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534812 true] [17592186198372 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311569 13194139534812 true] [17592186198372 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311590 13194139534812 true] [17592186198372 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311594 13194139534812 true] [17592186198372 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311597 13194139534812 true] [17592186198372 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311600 13194139534812 true] [17592186198373 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311555 13194139534812 true] [17592186198373 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311562 13194139534812 true] [17592186198373 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311603 13194139534812 true] [17592186198373 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311606 13194139534812 true] [17592186198374 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311576 13194139534812 true] [17592186198374 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311583 13194139534812 true] [17592186198374 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311610 13194139534812 true] [17592186198374 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311614 13194139534812 true] [17592186198374 1020 #edb/ref 17592186311617 13194139534812 true] [17592186198867 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534812 true] [17592186198867 1100 "Given that $P(A) = \\frac{1}{4}$, $P(B) = \\frac{1}{6}$, and $P(A∩B) = \\frac{1}{12}$, find $P(A^{′}∪B)$. Do not round your answer.$P(A^{′}∪B) =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534812 false] [17592186198867 1100 "Given that $P(A)=\\frac{1}{4},$ $P(B)=\\frac{1}{6},$ and $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{12},$ find $P({A}^{′}\\cup B).$ Do not round your answer.\n\n$P({A}^{′}\\cup B)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534812 true] [17592186198867 1145 "First, we calculate $P(A\\cup B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{12}+\\frac{2}{12}-\\frac{1}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{′}\\cup B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/0c8d9572472da406cf84f5657d0ea47d0d1ba76592c98d4e6f442ecb9ef03dec.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{′}\\cup B)=\\frac{1}{12}+\\frac{1}{12}+\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{5}{6}.\n$$" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311555 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311556 13194139534812 true] [17592186311555 1089 "q-120380" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311555 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534812 true] [17592186311555 1100 "Given that $P(A)=0.5,$ $P(B)=0.3,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.7,$ find $P({A}^{′}\\cup B).$" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311555 1113 #uuid "7e0fa3a1-48dc-5589-ad80-81b37d1c3742" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311555 1145 "First, we calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.7 & =0.5+0.3-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.5+0.3-0.7 \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{′}\\cup B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/14e573701578699d9c0fa5c0aa8f97d2c20fc916e867d0c89d3fe1256feccf69.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{′}\\cup B)=0.1+0.2+0.3=0.6.\n$$" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311557 13194139534812 true] [17592186311556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311558 13194139534812 true] [17592186311556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311559 13194139534812 true] [17592186311556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311560 13194139534812 true] [17592186311556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311561 13194139534812 true] [17592186311556 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534812 true] [17592186311556 1041 "selection" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311556 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311557 13194139534812 true] [17592186311556 1110 #uuid "1656c7a3-54a8-5ab1-8ab7-3fa4753b5a74" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311557 1034 "0.6" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534812 true] [17592186311557 1111 #uuid "85108317-0e0c-5754-8d3f-c1cf28245c8b" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311558 1034 "0.7" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311558 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534812 true] [17592186311558 1111 #uuid "c7a7080f-6088-5dee-bb0f-e3ec4a1c7f51" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311559 1034 "0.4" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311559 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534812 true] [17592186311559 1111 #uuid "e3a2198d-a0de-5f61-8913-352aaceaafdc" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311560 1034 "0.3" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534812 true] [17592186311560 1111 #uuid "4acc3406-4d3c-517f-a6a9-ca1de5d7a8db" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311561 1034 "0.5" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534812 true] [17592186311561 1111 #uuid "835d9ea6-5037-52bf-8833-7e880a957f5c" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311562 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311563 13194139534812 true] [17592186311562 1089 "q-178681" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311562 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534812 true] [17592186311562 1100 "Given that $P(A)=0.4,$ $P(B)=0.3,$ and $P(A\\cap B)=0.1,$ find $P({A}^{′}\\cup B).$" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311562 1113 #uuid "23d76757-31a5-5e79-8232-9c67b743d844" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311562 1145 "First, we calculate $P(A\\cup B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\  & =0.4+0.3-0.1 \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{′}\\cup B.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/e3fecd795207853d1a17a3e23c0d2872a59fde1c0561b8e357aae4a1705ca651.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP({A}^{′}\\cup B)=0.1+0.2+0.4=0.7.\n$$" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311563 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311564 13194139534812 true] [17592186311563 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311565 13194139534812 true] [17592186311563 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311566 13194139534812 true] [17592186311563 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311567 13194139534812 true] [17592186311563 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311568 13194139534812 true] [17592186311563 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534812 true] [17592186311563 1041 "selection" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311563 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311565 13194139534812 true] [17592186311563 1110 #uuid "07c30adf-7a65-52bb-ad05-421ab2128d13" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311564 1034 "0.6" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534812 true] [17592186311564 1111 #uuid "303b816f-884c-579e-9726-7d5c85ca6b7a" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311565 1034 "0.7" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311565 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534812 true] [17592186311565 1111 #uuid "a28b4b29-7b16-55b1-9658-122b0103a806" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311566 1034 "0.8" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311566 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534812 true] [17592186311566 1111 #uuid "2e8b2700-e01f-531e-a2ff-c84d068d7b27" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311567 1034 "0.5" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311567 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534812 true] [17592186311567 1111 #uuid "7d0801c9-297b-5bf2-859a