[17592186311606 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534812 true] [17592186311606 1100 "Given that $P(B)=\\frac{2}{5},$ $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{3},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{5}{6},$ find $P({A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}).$ Do not round your answer.\n\n$P({A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311606 1113 #uuid "0c42571e-fe28-594c-ae53-f8b3f913ae73" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311606 1145 "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{5}{6} & =P(A)+\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ P(A) & =\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{30}+\\frac{10}{30}-\\frac{12}{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region ${A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/4b5f335b449e5f07de1d9ac1590245e71f6825b2dc13fe4ba046985aac95465a.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}\\cup {B}^{′}) & =\\frac{13}{30}+\\frac{1}{15}+\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{30}+\\frac{2}{30}+\\frac{5}{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311607 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311608 13194139534812 true] [17592186311607 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311609 13194139534812 true] [17592186311607 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534812 true] [17592186311607 1041 "field-1" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311607 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311608 13194139534812 true] [17592186311607 1110 #uuid "c9e27fdb-5393-5bc6-b382-45d17479f361" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311608 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311608 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534812 true] [17592186311608 1111 #uuid "a347f503-e59c-596b-a7c3-13ce21105897" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311609 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311609 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534812 true] [17592186311609 1111 #uuid "8a647118-d024-5177-a8ec-298eb2d02e89" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311610 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311611 13194139534812 true] [17592186311610 1089 "q-264415" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311610 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534812 true] [17592186311610 1100 "Given that $P(A)=0.35,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.15,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.9,$ find $P({B}^{′}).$\n\n$P({B}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311610 1113 #uuid "de355132-c934-56e3-9f81-8d3f91957eb2" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311610 1145 "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.9 & =0.35+P(B)-0.15 \\\\ P(B) & =0.9+0.15-0.35 \\\\  & =0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({B}^{′}) & =1-P(B) \\\\  & =1-0.7 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311611 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311612 13194139534812 true] [17592186311611 1000 #edb/ref 17592186311613 13194139534812 true] [17592186311611 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534812 true] [17592186311611 1041 "field-1" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311611 1104 #edb/ref 17592186311613 13194139534812 true] [17592186311611 1110 #uuid "e433324a-9117-5f51-b34d-b07e9aab9098" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311612 1034 "0.7" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534812 true] [17592186311612 1111 #uuid "b16c18a4-c591-5800-8b60-5fbe6680ead6" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311613 1034 "0.3" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534812 true] [17592186311613 1111 #uuid "d1c040bc-c7a3-50b1-b43d-db040a876690" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311614 1017 #edb/ref 17592186311615 13194139534812 true] [17592186311614 1089 "q-264419" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311614 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534812 true] [17592186311614 1100 "Given that $P(A)=0.6,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.25,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.95,$ find $P({B}^{′}).$\n\n$P({B}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534812 true] [17592186311614 1113 #uuid "0dc08a